s with “Embedded map view (beta)” component.      Fix for failing to open regular page from modal page.      Fix for flow functions not working properly when navigation menu is disabled.      Fix for true/false value in nested object not getting changed via checkbox.      Fixes for component opacity functionality.      Fix for Lottie animation having a white background.      Fix dropdown's initial value \"Select option\" not working.      Fix for text decoration color and decoration style issues.      Fix for showing remaining audio loops and playing audio from a cached file.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3914 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Business Events\nDescription: You can now view the business events consumed by SAP Build Process Automation in the Acquired Events tile. See Manage Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-09\nValid as Of: 2023-11-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3915 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Cluster View\nDescription: You can now group instances based on attributes to analyze the process performance. See Gain Visibility Using Process Workspace.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-09\nValid as Of: 2023-11-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3916 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Generative AI Tutorial\nDescription: The tutorial Use Trial to Extract Information from Custom Documents with Generative AI and SAP Document AI is now available.  Learn how to use SAP Document AI with generative AI to automate the extraction of information from custom document types using large language models (LLMs).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-10\nValid as Of: 2023-11-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3917 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Removal of the Monitoring component\nDescription: As announced in January 2023 (see blog post and What's New), the Prometheus/Grafana installation that is part of the Monitoring component has been deprecated. The removal will happen with Kyma release 2.20.  Required action: If you haven’t started the transition to alternative solutions yet, please do it now. With the removal, you will lose the ability to browse for metrics in Grafana or call the Prometheus API directly.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-04\nValid as Of: 2023-11-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3918 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Extensibility Scenario Including the Customizing of Sequence and Resolution Determination\nDescription: You can now add custom logic to SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing by implementing extensions.   With the new extension, sequence and resolution can be determined automatically by a customer-specific implementation to simplify and optimize the maintenance of promotions.  For more information, see Getting Started with Extensibility for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing and Automatic Determination of Sequence and Resolution in the new Extensibility Guide for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3919 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data Access Service Supports OData V4\nDescription: The Data Access service for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing now also supports OData V4. With", ": Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3919 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data Access Service Supports OData V4\nDescription: The Data Access service for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing now also supports OData V4. With this, you can search for certain promotions assigned to specific subentities.  For more information, see Data Access.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3920 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deletion of All Regular Prices\nDescription: You can now delete all regular prices by using the new parameter cleanUpAll in combination with currentTimestamp.  For more information, see Administration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2481 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.16.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.14.0 to 2.16.0. Updated components:      com.sap.cloud.connectivity.apiext is updated from version 3.37.0 to 3.38.0      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 3.4.7 to 3.4.8      com.sap.hcp.cf.logging is updated from 3.8.3 to 3.8.4      otel-agent is updated from version 2.4.0 to 2.5.0      otel-agent-ext-java is updated from version 1.5.15 to 1.5.16    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2482 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of None Option for Onboarding Internal Repository with Hash Algorithms\nDescription: The None option has been deprecated from the selection of hashing algorithms in both Document Management Service, Integration Option and Document Management Service, Application Option.  See:    Onboard Repository in Document Management Service, Integration Option.      Onboarding Internal Repository in Document Management Service, Application Option.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2483 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Dev Plan update\nDescription: We have enabled storing audit logs for dev plan instances\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2484 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit,Usage Data Management\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Application Details Added to Monthly Usage Report API and Costs and Usage Spreadsheet\nDescription: We've added an application's details per usage record to the response field application in the GET /reports/v1/monthlyUsage API of the SAP Usage Data Management Service for SAP BTP.   We've also included the application's details to the exportable spreadsheet from the Costs and Usage page in the SAP BTP cockpit. You can find this in the Application Details column (O) in the Actual Usage tab. See Monitoring Usage and Consumption Costs in Your Global Account.  Note that this API field and spreadsheet column will be empty for services that don't report this information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-29\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2485 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Cloud Connector 2.17.1 - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Release of Cloud Connector version 2.17.1 provides the following bug fixes:      The subaccount authentication data expiration was not calculated correctly and reported as expired, even if still valid.      Regressions in 2.17.0:        LDAP secure host flags (Secure Host and Secure Alternate Host) were neither stored in the LDAP draft configuration nor in the final configuration when pressing the Save Draft or Activate button.      On the subaccount overview page, the region host could have been shown as not reachable with message Proxy could not be reached, even though the subaccount is shown as connected and there is no proxy in use. Productive connections were not affected.       Adding a subaccount was not possible, if BTP is reached only via a proxy and the proxy returns an unexpected status code on check.       CPIC trace files were neither shown nor downloadable from the UI.       The Open Shadow button at the top of the High Availability screen did not result in any action.       If adding an RFC SNC access control entry without load balancing logon, the virtual port had an additional 's' at the end. Such an entry could not be used from the cloud side.         These issues have been fixed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2486 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Cloud Connector 2.17.1 - Enhancements\nDescription: Release of Cloud Connector version 2.17.1 provides the following enhancement:    Additional filters were added in the access control table in which the mappings of virtual to internal systems are listed.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 